          "title": "You'll want to know: misslingen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "misslingen — \"to go wrong, to fail (of things)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Der erste Kuchen ist mir misslungen. My first cake went wrong."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Perfekt with sein: es ist misslungen. The thing is the subject and the person goes in the dative: Es misslingt mir."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "misslingen is built with miss- \"wrongly\" on the old verb behind gelingen \"to succeed\", Old High German gilingan, Proto-Germanic lingwaną (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
